From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:45:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 25/27] llama/server/sycl : keep decode-step data on the device

The decode step of MTP speculative decoding is GPU-bound; what is left
on the bus per step is moved to the device. Env switches, default off,
outputs unchanged:
- LLAMA_TGT_TOPK_DEVICE: the target's top-21 logits per row are selected
  on the device and only those are downloaded; the CPU sampler runs on
  them and reads the full row when values tie or a grammar / reasoning
  budget needs it (=2 verifies every row against the full-row path)
- LLAMA_KV_ROT_DEVICE: the rotation matrices of a quantized draft KV are
  uploaded once instead of before every graph
- GGML_SYCL_ASYNC_INPUTS=2: host-computed embedding rows are uploaded
  without waiting for the whole queue
- GGML_TRACE=<file>: GPU/host timeline of graphs and copies from the
  queue's completion events (no commands added to the queue)

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
